{#- Markdown cannot give a heading an id, so an empty HTML anchor goes before
    it. Several ids for one heading are possible, and they sit on consecutive
    lines so the block stays one thing.

    The single file writes every id a link inside it may point at: there, a link
    to another page of the manual stays inside the document and has to land
    somewhere. The per-page Markdown links to permalinks instead. Its heading
    carries one label as "{#...}", so it writes only the other labels of the
    section, as the HTML page does. -#}
{%- set anchorIds = env.outputFormat == 'singlemd' ? markdownSectionAnchors(node) : markdownLabelAnchors(node) -%}
{%- if anchorIds is not empty -%}
{% for anchorId in anchorIds %}<a id="{{ anchorId }}"></a>
{% endfor %}
{% endif -%}
{% for childNode in node.children -%}
    {{- renderNode(childNode) }}

{% endfor -%}
